<%# THE FUND-ACCOUNT CARD (onboarding step 2, main-account spec §5). One field — the account's
    real balance today, entered once as the ONE movement from main that mirrors the transfers
    that really happened over the years. Mirrors `_new_account`'s section chrome: same card
    shape, sitting where the "No pools in this account yet" line otherwise stands.

    Locals: `account` (an account-type Pool still awaiting its real balance — the render gate,
    `HomePresenter#awaiting_funding?`, lives in `_account.html.erb`), `movement`
    (HomePresenter#funding_movement_for's answer: the rejected
    PoolMovement if THIS is the card AccountFundingsController's 422 was for, a fresh unsaved
    one otherwise — the object `simple_form_for` is built on, so a refused amount and its error
    survive the re-render exactly as the add-account card's name does), `main_account` (the
    user's default account, passed rather than walked back to from `account.user` so this card
    costs no query of its own). %>
<%= simple_form_for movement, as: :account_funding, url: account_fundings_path do |f| %>
  <%= f.hidden_field :account_id, value: account.id %>
  <div class="px-6 py-4 flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-start gap-3">
    <div class="flex-1">
      <%= f.input :amount,
          as: :decimal,
          label: "Real balance today",
          placeholder: "0.00",
          input_html: { step: 0.01, min: 0.01 },
          hint: "One transfer from #{main_account.name} — match your bank statement." %>
    </div>
    <div class="sm:pt-7">
      <%= f.button :submit, "Fund account", class: "btn btn-primary" %>
    </div>
  </div>
<% end %>
